\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Worst-group robust potential}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{robustness}

\p{Let #{\mathcal G} be a declared finite family of evaluation groups, with
expected performance #{J_g(\pi;D,b)} for each #{g\in\mathcal G}. The
\strong{worst-group robust potential} is}

##{
 \Phi_{\mathrm{rob}}(M_0,B)
 =\sup_{\substack{P\in\mathfrak P(M_0),\ \operatorname{Trust}(P)\\
                  \mathbb E[C(P)]\leq B}}
   \min_{g\in\mathcal G}\mathbb E[J_g(\Pi_P;D,b)].
}

\p{Section 2 of \citef{sagawa2020distributionally} uses worst-group risk for
group shifts. The displayed maximization is an FTIP adaptation to independent
evaluation utility and lifecycle budgets.}

\p{The group family and its sampling law must be fixed before evaluation.
Worst-group performance can improve while average performance falls, so this
value is not interchangeable with scalarized average utility.}
